  levels:
  - icon: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 3675335aea8c98c4dac401c273f039b8, type: 3}
    title: Kepler's laws
    body: A simulation of a planet following all of Kepler's laws as it orbits the
      sun. Certain parameters can be manipulated to explore the physics the laws.
    sceneName: Earth Orbit 1
    isLocked: 0
  - icon: {fileID: -718923731338941120, guid: 3fe6587c6fd61e34f9aa695ff74f5cac, type: 3}
    title: Habitable Zone
    body: 'A simulation of the goldilocks zone (where the orbit of a planet has to
      be in order for there to be liquid water) around a star in 2D and 3D. '
    sceneName: Habitable Zone 1
    isLocked: 0
  - icon: {fileID: -6103562689817882513, guid: efa80e3119a312841bf99f5d33ce5682, type: 3}
    title: Mercury Perihelion Precession
    body: 'A simulation of mercury''s unique perihelion precession that helped prove
      Einsten''s theory of general relativity. '
    sceneName: MercuryOrbit_Adi
    isLocked: 0
  - icon: {fileID: 6926091425052019107, guid: e73e4a164c4915a42b58ae150c5d2537, type: 3}
    title: ISS Orbit
    body: A simulation of the famous ISS that tracks its location in realtime. You
      can also change the speed of it to simulate its movement over a longer period
      of time.
    sceneName: ISS
    isLocked: 0
  - icon: {fileID: 4565488893708855530, guid: ecadb6e7354540e418ab48b6b3b1cb17, type: 3}
    title: Stellar Evolution
    body: 'A simulation of a star''s life cycle over millions of years that changes
      based on the star''s inital mass. '
    sceneName: 
    isLocked: 0
